<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9986" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condemnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				condemning, condemnation</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecuniaria,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					2, 10, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">condemnationem facere,</span>”
				<i>to condemn</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib.
					42, 1, 59</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">or,</span>”
				<i>to bring about the condemnation of one</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 8, 14, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pati,</span>”
				<i>to be condemned</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					4, 2, 14</span></i>
			: post condemnationem, Gai <i><span class="en">Inst. 3,
			180</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">opp. absolutio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ascon. ad Cic. Div. in Caecil. 7,
				24</span></i>
			.</div>
